# Commit completed work

After finishing work the user asked for in this repository, commit it in the same turn. Do not wait for a separate request.

- Follow the repository git safety protocol. Do not push unless the user asks.
- Include the code, tests, assets and documentation that belong to the change.
- Leave out secrets, `.env` files, local editor state such as `.obsidian/workspace.json`, and unused files that are not part of the change.
- One commit per completed piece of work. If several finished pieces are still uncommitted, commit them together only when the user asks for everything outstanding.
